{
	"about": "The bucket and the pre-accept predicate, as a truth table. Published for the same reason the comparator is: the field contract was pinned once and two tracks still drifted on the thing the fields feed. clause_order is the strict precedence; cases drive validate_items.compute_initial_bucket() and assemble.apply_pre_accept() directly, and test_items.py asserts clause_order's length equals the number of return statements in the function, so a clause added without a fixture row is caught.",
	"d2_routing": "clause-2 guard (orchestrator ruling, overriding the spec's variants A and B): a barred security-only tool falls through to security_mixed — never to attention (A), and never left in security_auto with a cleared checkbox (B). security_mixed already renders an expanded card with an 'affects this setup' badge and correct counters; anything downstream of finalize_tool desyncs the Overview tiles.",
	"clause_order": [
		"0. content_losing(view) is non-empty -> attention   [D1 - above the source clause on purpose]",
		"1. source in NON_VERSION_SOURCES -> routine if expected else attention",
		"2. has_security and security_only and impact == \"none\" and version_delta not in (major, unknown) and runnable and not pre_accept_bars(view) -> security_auto   [D2/E3 - a barred tool falls through to security_mixed]",
		"3. has_security -> security_mixed",
		"4. risk_level elevated, or config needs_attention, or an edit/structural suggestion (items.needs_a_decision), or not runnable -> attention",
		"5. -> routine"
	],
	"pre_accept": "sug is baseline AND auto_runnable AND review_bucket != \"attention\" AND risk_level == \"low\" AND not content_losing(tool) AND not pre_accept_bars(tool)",
	"pre_accept_bars": {
		"order": [
			"elevated-risk",
			"reaches-item",
			"watch-hit"
		],
		"elevated-risk": "risk_level == \"elevated\" — bars everywhere (D2 core)",
		"reaches-item": "an item that ITSELF carries security content (the security tag, or a security block) with local.direction == \"reaches\" — the measured case: cask:wireshark-app's reaching item IS the security item. Never any reaching item, and never any reaching item on a security tool: the measurement was taken on security items only, and a re-widened predicate quietly un-compresses the routine population (919 words per decision is the number this redesign exists to kill)",
		"watch-hit": "any item carrying a watch_hit — a watch item exists to be told about, and one that fires into an auto-accepted card is inert (E3)"
	},
